  "arrangerNotes": "Refrain, vocal line, transcribed by visual reading of the original 1921 M. Witmark & Sons sheet music (page images and LilyPond transcription saved in scores/b9/scan/), key C major, cut time (durations in quarter-note beats; tempo is the quarter-note BPM), second ending. Simplification: the one D sharp ('fill me with EC-stasy', a chromatic note slurred down to D) is played as 2 (D). In the last phrase the sheet prints octave alternatives; the lower notes are used. Range 1 to high 3. D drum: the notes as written. C drum (no high 2 or 3): 'Oh, I'm just wild about Harry, And he's' is played an octave lower. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum).",
